    {
      "id": "interface",
      "layer": "interface",
      "summary": "CLI and lazy public API",
      "responsibilities": [
        "Dispatch native commands, list module contracts and render declared model trees or Mermaid without running unrelated owners Expose testfile manifest/check/inspect/diff/snapshot/series; retired dataset and coverage commands are absent. run --json exposes the full diagnostic report. Preflight reviews optionally accept --audit; mapping review is part of hierarchy evaluate. Describe a declared tree as text, full JSON or Mermaid and count observed mappings per block without solving or evaluating; expose mapping-summary counts in observed summaries",
        "Print a compact hierarchy/validation summary with derived names, check counts and assumption dispositions, and the full report with --json",
        "Write manifest source paths relative to the output manifest directory while preserving stdout-only path behavior",
        "Exit 0 on a passed check, 1 on a checked failure, and 2 when the command cannot run; comparison uses observed audit status",
        "Inspect assumption cards from either a single SystemSpec or the system inside a hierarchical audit",
        "Expose local/subtree verdicts, refinement consistency and per-template status in hierarchy summaries; pass the audit directory for file resolution",
        "Run hierarchy variants with optional fault compositions and observed signature matching; expose masked pairs, next signals and model misses without changing nominal inputs"
      ],
      "files": [
        "src/physicsguard/__init__.py",
        "src/physicsguard/cli.py",
        "src/physicsguard/core/__init__.py"
      ],
      "entrypoints": [
        "src/physicsguard/cli.py:main",
        "src/physicsguard/cli.py:build_parser"
      ],
      "state": [],
